_t *inputs,\0A    psa_pake_cipher_suite_t *cipher_suite);\0A\0A/** Set the session information for a password-authenticated key exchange.\0A *\0A * The sequence of operations to set up a password-authenticated key exchange\0A * is as follows:\0A * -# Allocate an operation object which will be passed to all the functions\0A *    listed here.\0A * -# Initialize the operation object with one of the methods described in the\0A *    documentation for #psa_pake_operation_t, e.g.\0A *    #PSA_PAKE_OPERATION_INIT.\0A * -# Call psa_pake_setup() to specify the cipher suite.\0A * -# Call \5Cc psa_pake_set_xxx() functions on the operation to complete the\0A *    setup. The exact sequence of \5Cc psa_pake_set_xxx() functions that needs\0A *    to be called depends on the algorithm in use.\0A *\0A * Refer to the documentation of individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX`\0A * values of type ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true)\0A * for more information.\0A *\0A * A typical sequence of calls to perform a password-authenticated key\0A * exchange:\0A * -# Call psa_pake_output(operation, #PSA_PAKE_STEP_KEY_SHARE, ...) to get the\0A *    key share that needs to be sent to the peer.\0A * -# Call psa_pake_input(operation, #PSA_PAKE_STEP_KEY_SHARE, ...) to provide\0A *    the key share that was received from the peer.\0A * -# Depending on the algorithm additional calls to psa_pake_output() and\0A *    psa_pake_input() might be necessary.\0A * -# Call psa_pake_get_implicit_key() for accessing the shared secret.\0A *\0A * Refer to the documentation of individual PAKE algorithm types (`PSA_ALG_XXX`\0A * values of type ::psa_algorithm_t such that #PSA_ALG_IS_PAKE(\5Cc alg) is true)\0A * for more information.\0A *\0A * If an error occurs at any step after a call to psa_pake_setup(),\0A * the operation will need to be reset by a call to psa_pake_abort(). The\0A * application may call psa_pake_abort() at any time after the operation\0A * has been initialized.\0A *